From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] user-command deadline: do not time out a command written
 during an idle wait

Upstream: https://github.com/wdoekes/asterisk-chan-dongle @ 31eb619600d5ce93237cd440c72db0bc33d7adfe
Purpose: an AtCommand is written by the AMI thread while the monitor thread
         already waits with its 10 s idle timeout, so the command timed out
         when that wait ended (after 0 to 10 s) and the modem was restarted,
         whatever Timeout it was given; an EC25 on LTE needs about 18 s for
         AT+CCFC (applies on top of 0002)

When the wait ends, a head command that was written and whose own deadline
is still ahead is waited for again instead of being reported as timed out.
---
 chan_dongle.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chan_dongle.c b/chan_dongle.c
index 8d4b36b..ba69560 100644
--- a/chan_dongle.c
+++ b/chan_dongle.c
@@ -518,6 +518,12 @@ static void* do_monitor_phone (void* data)
 		{
 			ast_mutex_lock (&pvt->lock);
 			ecmd = at_queue_head_cmd (pvt);
+			/* a command another thread wrote during this wait has a deadline of its own */
+			if(ecmd && ecmd->length == 0 && ast_tvdiff_ms (ecmd->timeout, ast_tvnow()) > 0)
+			{
+				ast_mutex_unlock (&pvt->lock);
+				continue;
+			}
 			if(ecmd)
 			{
 				ast_log (LOG_ERROR, "[%s] timedout while waiting '%s' in response to '%s'\n", dev, at_res2str (ecmd->res), at_cmd2str (ecmd->cmd));
